      <!-- SECTION 3 EN -->
      <h2 id="execution-lifecycle">03 · EXECUTION LIFECYCLE AND OMM ENGINE</h2>
      <p>What happens on Salesforce servers when an email send with AMPscript is triggered?</p>

      <div style="background:var(--bg-card); border:1px solid var(--border-dim); border-radius:var(--radius); padding:1.5rem; margin:1.5rem 0;">
        <div style="font-family:var(--font-arcade); font-size:0.5rem; color:var(--neon-pink); margin-bottom:1rem;">🔄 AN EMAIL'S JOURNEY: FROM CODE TO INBOX</div>
        
        <div style="display:flex; flex-direction:column; gap:0.9rem; font-size:0.88rem;">
          <div style="display:flex; align-items:flex-start; gap:0.8rem;">
            <span style="background:var(--neon-cyan); color:#000; font-family:var(--font-arcade); font-size:0.5rem; padding:0.2rem 0.5rem; border-radius:3px; flex-shrink:0;">STEP 1</span>
            <div><strong>Subscriber Context Initialization:</strong> The send engine loads a row from the target Data Extension or send list for the current subscriber.</div>
          </div>

          <div style="display:flex; align-items:flex-start; gap:0.8rem;">
            <span style="background:var(--neon-pink); color:#fff; font-family:var(--font-arcade); font-size:0.5rem; padding:0.2rem 0.5rem; border-radius:3px; flex-shrink:0;">STEP 2</span>
            <div><strong>OMM (Output Messaging Machine) Execution:</strong> The parser reads the email body <em>top-to-bottom</em>. It executes <code>%%[ ... ]%%</code> blocks, evaluates logic, and runs data queries.</div>
          </div>

          <div style="display:flex; align-items:flex-start; gap:0.8rem;">
            <span style="background:var(--neon-yellow); color:#000; font-family:var(--font-arcade); font-size:0.5rem; padding:0.2rem 0.5rem; border-radius:3px; flex-shrink:0;">STEP 3</span>
            <div><strong>Inline Injection:</strong> Output tags like <code>%%=v(@Name)=%%</code> are replaced with final HTML or text strings.</div>
          </div>

          <div style="display:flex; align-items:flex-start; gap:0.8rem;">
            <span style="background:var(--neon-green); color:#000; font-family:var(--font-arcade); font-size:0.5rem; padding:0.2rem 0.5rem; border-radius:3px; flex-shrink:0;">STEP 4</span>
            <div><strong>MTA Dispatch:</strong> The final rendered email (clean of any Marketing Cloud code) is dispatched to the recipient's mail server.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="callout tip">
        <div class="callout-label">💡 PRO TIP · CASE INSENSITIVITY</div>
        AMPscript is <strong>case-insensitive</strong>. <code>SET @name = "John"</code>, <code>set @Name = "John"</code> and <code>Set @NAME = "John"</code> are identical to the engine. However, adhering to standard conventions like <em>camelCase</em> ensures clean, maintainable code.
      </div>

      <!-- SECTION 4 EN -->
      <h2 id="basic-syntax">04 · BASIC SYNTAX AND DELIMITER TYPES</h2>
      <p>There are two primary ways to write AMPscript depending on your objective:</p>

      <h3>1. Multiline Code Blocks: <code>%%[ ... ]%%</code></h3>
      <p>Used for variable declarations, math operations, function calls, and conditional logic. Everything inside executes silently without rendering visible text.</p>

      <div class="code-block">
        <div class="code-block-header">
          <div class="code-block-dots"><div class="code-block-dot"></div><div class="code-block-dot"></div><div class="code-block-dot"></div></div>
          <span class="code-block-lang">AMPscript · Declaration & Assignment</span>
          <button class="code-copy-btn">📋 Copy</button>
        </div>
        <pre><span class="cm">%%[
  /* 1. Declare variables using the VAR keyword */</span>
  <span class="kw">VAR</span> <span class="vr">@name</span>, <span class="vr">@tier</span>, <span class="vr">@points</span>, <span class="vr">@discount</span>

  <span class="cm">/* 2. Assign values using SET */</span>
  <span class="kw">SET</span> <span class="vr">@name</span> = <span class="st">"Holwan David"</span>
  <span class="kw">SET</span> <span class="vr">@tier</span> = <span class="st">"VIP"</span>
  <span class="kw">SET</span> <span class="vr">@points</span> = <span class="nb">1250</span>

  <span class="cm">/* 3. Conditional logic */</span>
  <span class="kw">IF</span> <span class="vr">@tier</span> == <span class="st">"VIP"</span> <span class="kw">THEN</span>
    <span class="kw">SET</span> <span class="vr">@discount</span> = <span class="nb">20</span>
  <span class="kw">ELSE</span>
    <span class="kw">SET</span> <span class="vr">@discount</span> = <span class="nb">5</span>
  <span class="kw">ENDIF</span>
<span class="cm">]%%</span></pre>
      </div>

      <h3>2. Inline Output Delimiters: <code>%%= ... =%%</code></h3>
      <p>Used directly inside HTML tags or text paragraphs to <strong>output the value of a variable or function result</strong>:</p>

      <div class="code-block">
        <div class="code-block-header">
          <div class="code-block-dots"><div class="code-block-dot"></div><div class="code-block-dot"></div><div class="code-block-dot"></div></div>
          <span class="code-block-lang">HTML + Inline AMPscript</span>
          <button class="code-copy-btn">📋 Copy</button>
        </div>
        <pre><span class="cm">&lt;!-- Inline variable output in HTML --&gt;</span>
<span class="kw">&lt;h1&gt;</span>Hello, <span class="st">%%=v(@name)=%%</span>!<span class="kw">&lt;/h1&gt;</span>
<span class="kw">&lt;p&gt;</span>Your member tier is <span class="kw">&lt;strong&gt;</span><span class="st">%%=v(@tier)=%%</span><span class="kw">&lt;/strong&gt;</span>.<span class="kw">&lt;/p&gt;</span>
<span class="kw">&lt;p&gt;</span>You have a <span class="kw">&lt;span style="color:#00ffff;"&gt;</span><span class="st">%%=v(@discount)=%%</span> % discount<span class="kw">&lt;/span&gt;</span> available.<span class="kw">&lt;/p&gt;</span></pre>
      </div>

      <!-- SECTION 5 EN -->
      <h2 id="control-flow">05 · CONTROL FLOW: IF / ELSE CONDITIONAL STATEMENTS</h2>
      <p>Conditional logic enables dynamic content rendering tailored to each subscriber's unique profile:</p>

      <div class="code-block">
        <div class="code-block-header">
          <div class="code-block-dots"><div class="code-block-dot"></div><div class="code-block-dot"></div><div class="code-block-dot"></div></div>
          <span class="code-block-lang">AMPscript · IF / ELSEIF / ELSE Structure</span>
          <button class="code-copy-btn">📋 Copy</button>
        </div>
        <pre><span class="cm">%%[
  VAR @tier, @message

  SET @tier = AttributeValue("CustomerTier")

  IF @tier == "Platinum" THEN
    SET @message = "Exclusive VIP lounge access and unlimited free shipping."
  ELSEIF @tier == "Gold" THEN
    SET @message = "Enjoy a 15% discount on your next purchase."
  ELSE
    SET @message = "Earn reward points on every order to level up."
  ENDIF
]%%</span>

<span class="cm">&lt;!-- In email template --&gt;</span>
<span class="kw">&lt;div class="promo-box"&gt;</span>
  <span class="kw">&lt;p&gt;</span><span class="st">%%=v(@message)=%%</span><span class="kw">&lt;/p&gt;</span>
<span class="kw">&lt;/div&gt;</span></pre>
      </div>

      <!-- SECTION 6 EN -->
      <h2 id="essential-functions">06 · ESSENTIAL FUNCTIONS FOR YOUR EVERYDAY WORKFLOW</h2>
      <p>Key fundamental functions every SFMC developer must know:</p>

      <div style="display:grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(280px, 1fr)); gap: 1rem; margin: 1.5rem 0;">
        
        <div style="background:var(--bg-card); border:1px solid var(--border-dim); border-radius:var(--radius); padding:1rem;">
          <div style="font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.9rem; color:var(--neon-cyan); font-weight:700; margin-bottom:0.3rem;">AttributeValue("Field")</div>
          <p style="font-size:0.82rem; color:var(--text-secondary); margin:0;">Safely retrieves a subscriber attribute. If the field is missing or null, it returns an empty string instead of crashing the send.</p>
        </div>

        <div style="background:var(--bg-card); border:1px solid var(--border-dim); border-radius:var(--radius); padding:1rem;">
          <div style="font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.9rem; color:var(--neon-pink); font-weight:700; margin-bottom:0.3rem;">Empty(@var)</div>
          <p style="font-size:0.82rem; color:var(--text-secondary); margin:0;">Returns <code>True</code> if the variable is null, empty string, or undefined. Essential for defensive programming.</p>
        </div>

        <div style="background:var(--bg-card); border:1px solid var(--border-dim); border-radius:var(--radius); padding:1rem;">
          <div style="font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.9rem; color:var(--neon-yellow); font-weight:700; margin-bottom:0.3rem;">v(@var)</div>
          <p style="font-size:0.82rem; color:var(--text-secondary); margin:0;">Outputs variable content safely in inline mode.</p>
        </div>

        <div style="background:var(--bg-card); border:1px solid var(--border-dim); border-radius:var(--radius); padding:1rem;">
          <div style="font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.9rem; color:var(--neon-green); font-weight:700; margin-bottom:0.3rem;">Concat("Text1", @var, "Text2")</div>
          <p style="font-size:0.82rem; color:var(--text-secondary); margin:0;">Concatenates multiple strings and variables into a single result.</p>
        </div>

        <div style="background:var(--bg-card); border:1px solid var(--border-dim); border-radius:var(--radius); padding:1rem;">
          <div style="font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.9rem; color:var(--neon-purple); font-weight:700; margin-bottom:0.3rem;">ProperCase(@name)</div>
          <p style="font-size:0.82rem; color:var(--text-secondary); margin:0;">Capitalizes the first letter of each word. Perfect for cleaning messy raw database names.</p>
        </div>

        <div style="background:var(--bg-card); border:1px solid var(--border-dim); border-radius:var(--radius); padding:1rem;">
          <div style="font-family:var(--font-mono); font-size:0.9rem; color:var(--neon-cyan); font-weight:700; margin-bottom:0.3rem;">FormatDate(Now(), "yyyy-MM-dd")</div>
          <p style="font-size:0.82rem; color:var(--text-secondary); margin:0;">Formats date and time values into standardized readable patterns.</p>
        </div>

      </div>

      <!-- SECTION 7 EN · REAL USE CASES -->
      <h2 id="use-cases-en">07 · REAL USE CASES</h2>

      <div class="usecase-box">
        <div class="usecase-box-header">
          <span>✔️</span>
          <span>USE CASE: Dynamic Greeting with Safe Fallback</span>
        </div>
        <p style="font-size:0.88rem;color:var(--text-secondary);margin:0">
          Use <code>AttributeValue("FirstName")</code> with <code>Empty()</code> and <code>ProperCase()</code> to greet the recipient warmly by name or fallback cleanly to <em>"Valued Member"</em> when missing.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="usecase-box">
        <div class="usecase-box-header">
          <span>✔️</span>
          <span>USE CASE: Tiered Offers in Abandoned Cart Campaigns</span>
        </div>
        <p style="font-size:0.88rem;color:var(--text-secondary);margin:0">
          Evaluate cart value and customer tier (<code>IF @cartTotal > 100 AND @isVIP == "True"</code>) to display a 25% discount voucher with a trackable CTA button via <code>RedirectTo(@checkoutUrl)</code>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- SECTION 8 EN -->
      <h2 id="best-practices">08 · GOLDEN RULES FOR AMPSCRIPT DEVELOPMENT</h2>
      <ol style="padding-left:1.2rem; line-height:1.8; color:var(--text-secondary); font-size:0.9rem;">
        <li><strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">Always declare variables with <code>VAR</code>:</strong> Declaring variables at the top of your block prevents scoping issues and improves maintainability.</li>
        <li><strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">Wrap send context fields with <code>AttributeValue()</code>:</strong> Calling <code>[FieldName]</code> directly causes a hard send failure if the column doesn't exist in the Send DE. <code>AttributeValue()</code> fails safely.</li>
        <li><strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">Centralize control logic in the email header:</strong> Keep a primary <code>%%[ ... ]%%</code> block at the very top of your email and keep the HTML body clean with <code>%%=v(@var)=%%</code>.</li>
        <li><strong style="color:var(--text-primary);">Always test edge cases in Preview & Test:</strong> Verify behavior when a subscriber's first name or attribute is blank.</li>
      </ol>

      <div class="callout tip">
        <div class="callout-label">💡 PRO TIP · CODING CONVENTIONS</div>
        In our upcoming AMPscript guide, we will dive deep into <strong>Naming Conventions</strong>, variable prefixes (<code>@s_</code>, <code>@n_</code>, <code>@b_</code>), and modular Content Block architecture.
      </div>

      <!-- SECTION 9 · ARCADE CHALLENGE EN -->
      <h2 id="challenge-en">09 · ARCADE CHALLENGE: YOUR FIRST DYNAMIC GREETING</h2>
      <div class="challenge-box">
        <div class="challenge-box-header">
          <span class="challenge-box-icon">🎮 </span>
          <div>
            <div class="challenge-box-title">MISSION: Personalized Greeting with Discount</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <p style="font-size:0.9rem;color:var(--text-secondary);margin-bottom:1rem;">
          Create an AMPscript block that processes subscriber name (<code>FirstName</code>) and loyalty tier (<code>Tier</code>):
        </p>
        <ul style="font-size:0.88rem;color:var(--text-secondary);margin-bottom:1rem;">
          <li>If the name exists, format it in <strong>ProperCase</strong>; if blank, use the fallback <em>"Valued Member"</em>.</li>
          <li>If <code>Tier</code> is <strong>"VIP"</strong>, assign a 20% discount. If <strong>"Gold"</strong>, assign 10%. Otherwise, assign 5%.</li>
          <li>Output the greeting and discount voucher in the HTML.</li>
        </ul>

        <details style="font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:0.75rem;">
          <summary style="cursor:pointer;color:var(--neon-yellow);margin-bottom:0.75rem;"> View solution</summary>
          <div class="code-block" style="margin-top:0.75rem;">
            <div class="code-block-header">
              <div class="code-block-dots"><div class="code-block-dot"></div><div class="code-block-dot"></div><div class="code-block-dot"></div></div>
              <span class="code-block-lang">Full Solution · AMPscript</span>
              <button class="code-copy-btn">📋 Copy</button>
            </div>
            <pre><span class="cm">%%[
  /* 1. Declare all variables */</span>
  <span class="kw">VAR</span> <span class="vr">@rawName</span>, <span class="vr">@formattedName</span>, <span class="vr">@tier</span>, <span class="vr">@discountPercent</span>

  <span class="cm">/* 2. Safely extract subscriber data */</span>
  <span class="kw">SET</span> <span class="vr">@rawName</span> = <span class="fn">AttributeValue</span>(<span class="st">"FirstName"</span>)
  <span class="kw">SET</span> <span class="vr">@tier</span> = <span class="fn">AttributeValue</span>(<span class="st">"Tier"</span>)

  <span class="cm">/* 3. Validate and format name with Empty() */</span>
  <span class="kw">IF NOT EMPTY</span>(<span class="vr">@rawName</span>) <span class="kw">THEN</span>
    <span class="kw">SET</span> <span class="vr">@formattedName</span> = <span class="fn">ProperCase</span>(<span class="vr">@rawName</span>)
  <span class="kw">ELSE</span>
    <span class="kw">SET</span> <span class="vr">@formattedName</span> = <span class="st">"Valued Member"</span>
  <span class="kw">ENDIF</span>

  <span class="cm">/* 4. Evaluate tier and assign discount */</span>
  <span class="kw">IF</span> <span class="vr">@tier</span> == <span class="st">"VIP"</span> <span class="kw">THEN</span>
    <span class="kw">SET</span> <span class="vr">@discountPercent</span> = <span class="nb">20</span>
  <span class="kw">ELSEIF</span> <span class="vr">@tier</span> == <span class="st">"Gold"</span> <span class="kw">THEN</span>
    <span class="kw">SET</span> <span class="vr">@discountPercent</span> = <span class="nb">10</span>
  <span class="kw">ELSE</span>
    <span class="kw">SET</span> <span class="vr">@discountPercent</span> = <span class="nb">5</span>
  <span class="kw">ENDIF</span>
<span class="cm">]%%</span>

<span class="cm">&lt;!-- Rendered HTML --&gt;</span>
<span class="kw">&lt;div style="background:#1a1d2e; border:1px solid #00ffff; border-radius:8px; padding:20px; font-family:sans-serif; color:#ffffff;"&gt;</span>
  <span class="kw">&lt;h2 style="color:#00ffff; margin-top:0;"&gt;</span>Hello, <span class="st">%%=v(@formattedName)=%%</span>!<span class="kw">&lt;/h2&gt;</span>
  <span class="kw">&lt;p&gt;</span>As a valued member of our community, you have a special perk:<span class="kw">&lt;/p&gt;</span>
  <span class="kw">&lt;div style="font-size:24px; font-weight:bold; color:#ff00ff;"&gt;</span>
    🎟️ <span class="st">%%=v(@discountPercent)=%%</span> % OFF
  <span class="kw">&lt;/div&gt;</span>
<span class="kw">&lt;/div&gt;</span></pre>
          </div>
          <p style="margin-top:0.8rem; font-size:0.85rem; color:var(--text-secondary);">
            <strong>Breakdown:</strong> We use <code>AttributeValue()</code> to prevent send errors on missing fields. With <code>IF NOT EMPTY()</code> we format the name using <code>ProperCase()</code>, and finally evaluate <code>@tier</code> with clean conditional statements.
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>

    </div>

